Richard
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

# --- COLOR ---
# [] brass throat-button stamped with the Kesharat mark, worn smooth at the edge from repeated brushing
# [] tea kettle with a chipped spout, its handle wrapped in fraying twine
# [] Richard's left boot heel split open, leather flared outward from repeated treading on rock
# [] neck cloth loose at the collar, revealing a line of grassland sunburn that fades into dry mesa tan
# [] hands of a farmer — calloused, knuckles swollen, nails dark with soil still under the cuticles
# [] laminated activation card folded precisely in half, corners worn down to the paper grain
# [] Richard's voice shifting mid-sentence from coarse farmer cadence to precise technical register
# [] kettle hanging over the fire without a tripod, balanced on a bent wire loop
# [] hatband of Veran's felt hat dusty at the inside fold, no sweat ring despite the heat
# [] Richard's fingers tapping a slow rhythm on his knee — three quick, one long — while he talks about the pig
# [] a single bent wire from the cable run caught in the scree near the pylon's base, rusted at the tip
# --- end ---

FIXME(mundane): Richard is still on his brother's husbandry, telling you what the pig should be eating and what he suspects his brother is actually feeding her. He is genuinely worried about it.

FIXME(dread): You ask him about the tower. His voice shifts mid-sentence. He becomes precise. He talks about propagation, tolerances, schedule margins, the activation sequence. The technical fluency is fluent. The details are wrong in small confident ways. Real communications relays do not work the way he is describing. Neither Richard nor the others notice the shift. When he finishes he goes back to the pig.

FIXME(dread): You ask him how a pig farmer from Aldgate came to be running activation sequences on a mesa. Richard blanks. His eyes go somewhere middle-distance and he starts a sentence and does not finish it.

FIXME(dread): Veran steps in to save him. He says the Kesharat training program is the finest on the continent: bright young men like Richard come through the regional academy in eight weeks and are calibrating carrier-frequency drift by the end of the second. He says it the way a man says it who has trained other men.

FIXME(dread): Then Veran turns to you. He says you strike him as someone who would do well in the program. The autumn cohort at Hesh is still taking names. He says it without urgency, in the same tone he just used about Richard, as if mentioning a road that goes somewhere useful you might not have known about. Richard nods along. The blank does not entirely leave him. Veran goes back to his tea. Richard finds his way back to the pig.

choices:

* Step back to the circle = Let the conversation end
    +add_tag signal_array.met_richard
    +open "The Rest Interval"
